experiment: phaseteach
  phaseteach -- can a taught utterance occupy two phases of the
  creature's own free-running F1 gesture?
  the quantity  produced F1 in phase 1 minus produced F1 in phase 0
  the evidence  the DIFFERENCE between the two mappings, because the
                oscillator contributes to both equally and cancels
  refused if    the two mappings come back equal, or ph_off is not ~0,
                or ph_share is near 0 or 1 (a settled winner, not an
                alternation, and one phase bin nearly empty)


  arm           n     F1 ph0    F1 ph1  separation (ph1-ph0)    share    off  err drop (early-late)
  fixed         0          -         -  (one phase bin empty)    0.00   0.00  +0.2197 +/- 0.0120  
  phase         0          -         -  (one phase bin empty)    0.00   1.00  +0.0006 +/- 0.0025  
  phase-sw      0          -         -  (one phase bin empty)    0.00   1.00  +0.0006 +/- 0.0025  
  fast          0          -         -  (one phase bin empty)    0.00   1.00  +0.0003 +/- 0.0025  
  fast-sw       0          -         -  (one phase bin empty)    0.00   1.00  +0.0003 +/- 0.0025  
  DID THE LESSON LAND     error early minus late on `fixed`, whose target does NOT
                          flip within a trial:  +0.2197 +/- 0.0120  (18.4 SE, n=18)
  CREDIT RESOLUTION  vocal tau_elig 2000 ms (global 2000 x scale 1.000) against a phase of ~334 ms  ->  6.0 phases per trace
  CREDIT DELIVERY    of the credit standing at the event, the share left when the praise lands:
                      500 ms teacher   77.9%          50 ms teacher   97.5%

  phaseteach VOID -- THE REWARD CANNOT RESOLVE THE PHASE. The
  eligibility trace spans 6.0 phases, so both halves of the gesture
  are equally eligible on every praise event and the two mappings are
  the same experiment with the labels permuted. A null here would say
  nothing about whether a lesson can aim a gesture.

  THIS IS NOT A POWER PROBLEM and more creatures cannot fix it. It
  needs a credit window SHORTER THAN A PHASE, which means temporal
  credit assignment -- the spatial credit problem on the time axis,
  and the project's state persistence (~10 ms) is 200x shorter than
  its credit window. The gesture sits between the two, reachable by
  neither.
